{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And seal.</b> A verb; the sense is ונחתום (let it be sealed), patterned like כי נכסוף נכספת (for I have deeply longed). One may ask why Mordecai wrote to kill the enemies of the Jews — was it not enough for him and for them that they be saved? Know that he was a great sage, and Ahasuerus said to him, with all that you can, to deliver your people, for the earlier letters that Haman wrote were written in my name and sealed with my ring; I cannot revoke them, for such is the law of Media and Persia. And the proof is from the words of Daniel, that Darius could not save him. And Mordecai was compelled to write accordingly. Know that the king commanded Haman, who was second to the king, to write letters in the king's name, and the king gave him his ring to seal with them, that the Jews should kill their enemies on the thirteenth of the month of Adar. But Haman reversed the matter, that the Jews should be killed on the aforementioned day. And since he [the king] knew of his going about his evil plan, he hanged him on the tree, because he had sent his hand against the Jews, contrary to the king's will. And this is the meaning of ובבאה לפני המלך (and when she came before the king), as I will explain. And behold, the trustworthy proof is that Haman was hanged, and the king commanded other letters to be written and they were sealed with his [the king's] ring, according to his original will. And this is the meaning of ונפוץ (and it went forth)."], :book :esther, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {0 "The final word is given as ונפוך in the Hebrew text, but Ibn Ezra's argument requires ונפוץ from Esther 8:17; translated accordingly. The verse reference 'Esther 8:8' supplied for this comment is slightly mismatched, as the lemma ונחתום appears at 8:8 but the discussion extends to 8:10–17."}, :source-witnesses [["Kol Sason, Krotoschin, 1840" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001728315"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:30:20.535549574Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}